 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "balls is a list of integers (positive or negative). Two players alternate, the first player moving first. On a turn the player takes 1 or 2 balls from the left end, or 1 or 2 balls from the right end, of the remaining line (never one from each end in the same turn), and adds their values to their score. Both play optimally to maximise their own final score (equivalently the score difference, because the total is fixed). Return the first player's final score. An empty line returns 0.",
